{#- #885, out of #87. The partner programme, rented from Rewardful (operator,
    29 Sep 2026: "we can build out rewardful but put a 'coming soon' notice
    when I actually onboard with them and have customers, rather than beta").

    Two states, decided by one build-time fact, `rewardful.on`
    (src/_data/rewardful.js, true only when REWARDFUL_API_KEY is set):

      DARK  one line, *Coming soon*, nothing else. The page is noindex
            (partners.11tydata.js) and out of the sitemap, so search is not
            asked to rank a sentence.
      LIT   the seven terms from docs/research/partner-programme.md in the
            studio repo, in the words a partner reads, and one way in: the
            Rewardful signup link when REWARDFUL_SIGNUP_URL is set, else our
            address.

    The rate, the twelve months and the thirty-day hold are set inside
    Rewardful by #886 and quoted here; the cookie window and the attribution
    rule are set there too, which is why rule 3 states no number of days.
    English only, like the legal pages: these are terms, and a translation
    of terms is a compliance job, not a catalogue entry. -#}

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">partners</span>
    {%- if rewardful.on %}
    <h1 class="page-h1">Refer a client, earn 20% for a year.</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      An agency gets 20% either way, and a workspace only ever earns one of the two.
      Pay for a workspace you run for your own clients and it is 20% off.
      Send a client who pays us directly and you get 20% of what they pay, for their first twelve months.
    </p>
    {%- else %}
    <h1 class="page-h1">Coming soon.</h1>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>

{%- if rewardful.on %}
<section class="section">
  <div class="legal-inner">
    <h2 class="section-h2">The terms</h2>
    <ol class="partner-terms">
      <li>You cannot refer yourself: not your own domain, your own workspace, your own card, or an address at your company.</li>
      <li>A company that has ever had a workspace cannot be referred. Deleted counts as ever.</li>
      <li>The first partner link a buyer used is the one that counts. One partner per workspace.</li>
      <li>A workspace you pay for at 20% off does not also earn 20% back.</li>
      <li>No ads on our name, and no coupon sites.</li>
      <li>We can end a partnership and cancel unpaid earnings if the rules are broken.</li>
      <li>Earnings become payable thirty days after the invoice they come from is paid, and are paid out through Rewardful.</li>
    </ol>
    {%- if rewardful.signup %}
    <p><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ rewardful.signup }}" rel="noopener">Sign up as a partner</a></p>
    {%- else %}
    <p>Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we send you your link.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="partner-note">Your link and your balance are in Rewardful, which runs the programme for us. What its cookie records, and how to switch it off, is in <a href="/privacy/#cookies">the privacy notice</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
